>> title: Apple Cider Pork Chops
>> servings: 4
>> author: Ted Lin
>> date: 2019-01-19
>> dish: pork chops
>> course: main
>> keywords: pork, apple
>> summary: Pork chops cooked in apple cider until sweet and tender.
>> modified: 2026-11-04

# Pork

:season @{pork chop|4|sirloin-end} with @salt and @{black pepper} => _pork.
:coat _pork lightly with @flour, then let rest.
:heat #{skillet|high} with @oil or @butter.
:brown _pork on both sides in #skillet, about 1 min per side; remove the pork from the skillet.

# Sauce

:cook @{onion|1|sliced}, @{apple|2|small, sliced} in #skillet until the onions start to caramelize => _{onions and apples}.
:{simmer|15-20 min} _pork, _{onions and apples}, @{sage|1 tsp}, @{apple cider|1 cup} in #skillet => _braise.
:lift the pork out of _braise, and the apples too if you do not want them mushy, leaving the sauce in the skillet => _chops + _sauce.
:simmer _sauce until the liquid reduces; add @cream to thicken.
:return _chops to _sauce to bring back to temperature before serving.
:serve _chops and _sauce with the apples.

>> note: Serve with a baked potato and salad greens.
>> note: Rosemary also works, added or used instead of the sage.
